  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "LESSON XXVII"
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "text": "CULTURAL NOTE"
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "text": "MEDICAL CARE"
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "text": "Although large single-building hospitals can be found in many Italian cities, it is more normal to find Italian university hospitals or large city hospitals located in several buildings, each with its own medical specialization."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "text": "City hospitals or university hospitals are non-profit organizations run by the local government."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "text": "In Italy there is a National Health Insurance Plan for all citizens that covers most medical and hospital expenses."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "text": "However, in addition to their belonging to the National Health Service, some physicians also maintain a private practice."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "text": "Cliniche (private hospitals) are usually smaller and more luxurious but not necessarily as well staffed and equipped as public hospitals."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "text": "Emergencies are handled either by the Croce Rossa (Red Cross) or the Croce Verde (Green Cross) ambulance service."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "text": "Unless a specific request is made, either Croce Rossa or Croce Verde will take a patient to the emergency room of the nearest hospital."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "text": "In case of emergency one should first call his/her medico di fiducia (family doctor)."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "text": "However, very often, if out of the office, the doctor leaves a recording with the name and telephone number of a substitute."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "text": "If no answer is obtained, one may look in the daily newspaper and find a list of duty doctors assigned to various sections of the city."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "text": "Infermiere/a (nurse) is a general term for anyone involved in patient care at any level of nursing."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "text": "The term infermiere/a does not automatically imply that a person has the formal equivalent education of an R.N. or an L.P.N."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 16,
      "text": "Infermieri/e with more formal nursing education are called assistenti sanitari/sanitarie."
    },
    {
      "sequence_id": 17,
      "text": "Private-duty nurses are also available."
    }
  ],
